t(24, 800, """The success granted by Allah the Almighty is the greatest of the secrets of the earth; not your mind, not your body, not your clan, not people's support for you, nor the means responding to you, because much of the means' response is trial and gradual entrapment .. The proof of success is not outward success .. money .. business .. villa .. luxury car .. all this is wrong understanding .. The proof of success is the soul at peace in the abode of this world .. and the wretched, miserable, very poor man's soul is not at peace until he is content .. Sufficiency is not luxury; Allah Most High created us to live with sufficiency, neither poor nor destitute, and this is what the Prophet ﷺ and his family taught us. So success is contentment with sufficiency, and sufficiency with contentment, so the soul is at peace. I have long known owners of wealth whose days are anxiety and whose nights are sleeplessness! Is this success? No, by Allah .. this is a show of success; they act out to people that they are successful and act out to people that they are happy, but most people do not know. How far apart are one who knows things and their reality and one ignorant of them, deceived! As for Qarun, he was never successful; so take heed, for a believer should not be a fool!""")

h(24, 1500, """The greatest of the secrets of the earth!""")

t(24, 2315, """A Mighty, Generous Lord; when He sent the messengers and the books, that was a great pampering for humans and with them the jinn .. The Mighty Lord cares for the affair of His servants .. He cares for their happiness in this world and the Hereafter .. But most people did not see this pampering and did not take it in; they did not understand it and, sadly, did not grasp the truth that it was indeed pampering and indulgence; they took it as punishment and deprivation of the forbidden pleasures they craved. So they erred in understanding their Generous Lord, did not understand their lives as they should and must, and therefore did not live a good, pure, clean, wholesome life. For what they thought was restriction was always pampering since Adam, peace be upon him, because our Mighty Lord wanted us to live in villas and palaces, to eat without getting tired, to eat and be healthy, not to hate one another and not to quarrel, and for people to enjoy thousands of beautiful things. Our Mighty Lord decreed that His pious servants …""")

t(25, 60, """… would live a good life in the abode of this world. But people did not see the Qur'an as a letter of love and affection from Allah; most of them, not all, saw it as a letter of restriction and control. So they grew restless and fled from their Lord like a runaway slave in the bygone eras of slavery; slaves of ill omen whispered in his ears and told him: "There is no life for us with our masters; freedom is better than them." They hurried their steps by night, and highwaymen met them and enslaved them anew, though yesterday they had been honored by masters who treated them as a patron treats, not as one treats a slave. Servitude to Allah Most High is the only servitude that is complete honor, perfect might and decisive triumph. For we are truly servants of Allah our Mighty Lord, but His great teachings make us live on earth as honored masters; our Mighty Lord supports us, when we obey Him, with mastery, might and high worth. And this is something the runaway from Allah's Book, who sees Allah's Book as prison chains, attains nothing of; he will live forever with no direction and no path that leads him anywhere but to the mirage.""")

h(25, 800, """The command to every beautiful thing, as in our Lord's Book, makes the revelation of the Qur'an to humanity the peak of humanity's pampering with Allah Most High""")

