t(30, 515, """What I told young people in many old recordings: the old question, why is water cheap and diamonds expensive, is exactly what must be understood about the concept of marginal value in pricing. Therefore life, in its means and the movement of its means, rests in large part on the concept of marginal value: water is very plentiful and obtainable, so its price is cheap, while diamonds are rare and not plentiful like water, so their price is very high. That is why the young person must realize the difference between not building and building, ignorance and knowledge, lack of abilities and abilities, and build himself and his own being. For the construction worker works with far greater effort than an employee with mental skills, yet the construction worker's wage is far less than the employee's salary.""")

