t(35, 2550, """An angry person commented, objecting to my saying that it is not permissible to say of a dead person "he is being held to account now"

Learn the answer and do not sanctify people; a charitable person is not sanctified in his ignorance!""")

t(36, 95, """Answer: It is not permissible for a person to assert with certainty that a specific person is being held to account now in a specific way. Among scholars this is called "presuming upon Allah." It came in the authentic hadith that a man said: "By Allah, Allah will not forgive so-and-so," and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: "Who is this who swears by Me that I will not forgive so-and-so? I have forgiven him and annulled your deeds."

Summary: It is not valid in Sharia to "assert" with certainty the details of what happens to the dead, because they are of the unseen. The right word is to pray for him for steadfastness and mercy, and to avoid expressions that suggest knowledge of Allah's judgment on His servants.""")

h(36, 800, """An objection from an angry person. Presuming upon Allah in someone's saying: "So-and-so is being held to account now!" """)

